OL,3,ABowie house plan too big for street,
OL,4,Alocals say
OL,5,
OL,6,FPeople living near David Bowie's
OL,7,Fsouth-east London childhood home have
OL,8,Fobjected to plans to turn it into a
OL,9,Fvisitor attraction, saying a scheme
OL,10,Fexpected to draw 20,000 people a year
OL,11,Fis too much for a quiet suburban
OL,12,Fstreet.
OL,14,FThe Heritage of London Trust (HOLT) has
OL,15,Fapplied to Bromley Council to restore 4
OL,16,FPlaistow Grove, where Bowie lived from
OL,17,Fthe age of eight to 20, and build a
OL,18,Fvisitor centre in the garden.
OL,20,FResidents say the entrance, parking and
OL,21,Fevening events have not been thought
OL,22,Fthrough.
OL,23,APub: 27-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,311,300,200,140,0,100
